# Union merge applies to the APPEND-ONLY docs only. Two people write to the tail of the same file
# from separate machines, which is the most conflict-prone shape in git, so `decisions.md` and
# `collab.md` use git's built-in `union` driver: both sides' lines are kept, no conflict markers.
#
# NARROWED 2026-08-04. This previously covered all five persistent docs, `.claude/work/*.md`.
# Three of them — issues.md, hotfixes.md, traps.md — are CHURN lists, where deleting an entry is a
# normal operation ("an entry leaves the moment it is filed"; "remove entries whose hotfix is gone
# from the tree"). Union merge cannot express a deletion. A one-sided delete survives, but a delete
# that races with any edit to the same region is silently DISCARDED and the entry comes back —
# measured 2026-08-04. The worst case is hotfixes.md: you remove an entry because you reverted the
# code, the other owner adds a `Last checked:` line to it, and the merge resurrects an entry
# claiming a hotfix is in the tree that is not. Those three now take git's normal 3-way merge, so a
# concurrent append CONFLICTS and is resolved by hand. That is the trade: loud and occasional,
# rather than silent and wrong.
#
# The cost of union, on the two files that keep it: it NEVER conflicts. Measured 2026-07-31, two
# entries with distinct text merge correctly (only the blank line between them is eaten, being
# common to both sides), but lines that are byte-IDENTICAL on both sides are deduplicated and the
# two entries interleave into one block that reads as coherent and is not. Measured again
# 2026-08-04, the inverse: two people editing the SAME existing line makes union keep BOTH
# versions, reported as one insertion, no conflict. So every entry carries a `— <author>` stamp and
# a time, entries are appended rather than edited, and an in-place amendment is announced in
# collab.md first. See .claude/CLAUDE.md, "Formatting for union merge", and .claude/work/traps.md.
#
# Deliberately NOT covered: work/current/ (gitignored, per-person) and work/archive/ (write-once
# per task directory, so it cannot collide). Note gitattributes globs do not cross `/`, so
# `.claude/work/*.md` reaches only files directly in work/ — confirm with `git check-attr merge -- <path>`.
#
# Also deliberately absent, added 2026-08-11: `deferred.md`. Stated here because "not listed" and
# "nobody considered it" look identical in this file. It is a churn list by the same test as the
# three narrowed above — an entry is DELETED when it graduates to a GitHub issue — so it takes the
# normal 3-way merge and a concurrent append conflicts. Do not add a union line for it.
.claude/work/decisions.md merge=union
.claude/work/collab.md merge=union

# Shell scripts are checked out with LF regardless of core.autocrlf. Added 2026-08-13 — Michael,
# after `sudo ./serve.sh` in WSL failed with `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`.
# Both owners' Windows clones have core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every .sh to CRLF on
# checkout; the shebang then names an interpreter called `bash\r`, which does not exist. The
# hooks in .claude/hooks/ dodged this only because the harness invokes them as `bash <script>`,
# where the shebang is never read — they were CRLF too. Without this line the fix is not durable:
# the next checkout, merge or stash puts the CRs straight back.
*.sh text eol=lf
